    | | |__|__| | |             |___  |     4 - Gaia Blade
    | |         | |                 | |     5 - Tourniquet x2</pre>
      </AsciiMap>
      <AsciiMap>
<pre>_| |_     ___| |    _______   ___| |                _
  |     |   | ____|   | S    _   ___ *|               |5|
  |____ |   |____ |   |____ |     __| |___   _________| |
  | ____|   |* ___|   |  ___|    |    ____   ___________|
  |____ |   | |       | |        |4  |
  |  ___|   |  \_____/* |        |___|
  | |        \___   ___/
__| |            | |              ____
__  |                            |  __
  | |___   ____  | |        __   | |
  |_____   __  | | |__   __/  \__| |
             | |_|  __   _________*/
             |_____|</pre>
      </AsciiMap>
      <p>Many enemies here are weak to fire, so Stocke&#x27;s new <Tag type="weapon">Wisp Blade</Tag> can be very useful in the right battles. Eruca&#x27;s <Tag type="skill">Burst Light</Tag> can also be quite obscene. At the fork, head south, then east two screens where you will bump into <Tag type="char">Liese</Tag>. Talk to her to advance the [Mankind &amp; Beastkind] sidequest.</p>
      <p>Return to the entrance and follow the northern path to the next screen until you reach an open area. In the lower left corner is a chest which contains a <Tag type="acc">Beast Charm</Tag> (ATK+10) that you should save for later. Examine the corpse in the upper right corner to advance the [Mankind &amp; Beastkind] sidequest. Open the hidden chest next to him which contains the <Tag type="key">Roll-Cut Scroll</Tag> for <Tag type="char">Marco</Tag>. Return to Liese once more to advance the [Mankind &amp; Beastkind] sidequest.</p>
      <p>I would strongly recommend leaving and completing some sidequests at this time, since the rewards are really good, and the next couple areas are a little tough. Return to &quot;A New Mission&quot; to teach that new scroll to <Tag type="char">Marco</Tag> and to &quot;The Three Contracts&quot; to teach the new Pact to <Tag type="char">Aht</Tag>. Return to the &quot;Echoing Hills&quot; node and defeat the bandits again. Talk to <Tag type="char">Tarquin</Tag> to advance the [Mercenary Recruit] sidequest.</p>
      <p>Return to the &quot;Castle Sewers&quot; node and talk to <Tag type="char">Liese</Tag> in the northwest corner of the Downtown area to be prompted for a decision. Choosing to &quot;Leave it to her&quot; will unlock the [Chains of Hatred] ending. Instead, return to the decision point and choose to &quot;Believe in him&quot; to advance the [Mankind &amp; Beastkind] sidequest. Talk to the soldier by the save point on Main Street to complete the [Mankind &amp; Beastkind] sidequest and receive the <Tag type="weapon">Promised Knife</Tag> (ATK+27/MAG+75/HP-30, equip on <Tag type="char">Aht</Tag>). Aht should now be able to one shot almost everything with her <Tag type="skill">Cross Star</Tag> spell.</p>
      <p>Return to &quot;The Resistance&quot; node and talk to <Tag type="char">Will</Tag>, giving him the <Tag type="key">Sand Sword</Tag> and receiving <Tag type="gold">1500 G</Tag>. Like with the Escort event earlier, you don&#x27;t have to do it now, but if you don&#x27;t, you will have to do it sooner or later anyway. This will also enable you to unlock two rather obscure nodes, as well.</p>
      <p>Continue the plot to the &quot;Capital in Flames&quot; node at <Tag type="place">Granorg</Tag>. Walk north until you automatically talk to Will to unlock the [Will&#x27;s Sword] node. Return to the &quot;Wounded Otto&quot; node and continue the plot through the <Tag type="place">Sand Fortress</Tag> to unlock the [Will to the Rescue] node.</p>
      <p>Return to the &quot;Waiting at Skalla&quot; node and proceed to <Tag type="place">Skalla</Tag>, as before. Talk to Tarquin to advance the [Mercenary Recruit] sidequest. Proceed with events as before until you make it back to the <Tag type="place">Abyssia Forest</Tag>.</p>
      <p>Follow the lower path east one screen to a fork. If you like, head east to see how Liese&#x27;s relationship is going. Otherwise, head north. Follow the left path to the next area where there is a chest which contains a <Tag type="item">Healing Fruit</Tag>. Go back to the fork and take the right path to the next area.</p>
      <p>There is another fork ahead. After clearing the enemies, search behind the trees on the lower left side for a barrel. Move it down to the rocks along the lower path to gain access to another small area. Search around for a hidden chest which contains the <Tag type="weapon">Gaia Blade</Tag> (ATK+30/MAG+25/HP+100, equip on <Tag type="char">Marco</Tag>).</p>
      <p>Continue east to a long road of tall grass. At the end of the path is a dead end with a chest which contains <Tag type="item">2 Tourniquets</Tag>. Return to the last fork and follow the northern path to the ruins. You should rest up at <Tag type="place">Skalla</Tag> before entering, first.</p>
      <Callout type="note" title="Recommended Equipment">
        <p>Recommended Equipment at this point in the game:<br/>
        <strong>Stocke:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Pieti Edge</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Moirae Manteau</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Crystal Charm x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Raynie:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Witch Spear</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Sable Larme</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Crystal Charm x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Marco:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Gaia Blade</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Tungsten Mail</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Bishop Stud x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Aht:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Promised Knife</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Life Robe</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Bishop Stud x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Eruca:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Freikugel Kreuz</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Rune Dress</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Crystal Charm x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Extra:</strong> <Tag type="armor">Gospel Armor</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Beast Charm</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">5 Iron Charms</Tag></p>
      </Callout>
    </div>
  </ChapterCard>

  <!-- Chapter 46 -->
  <ChapterCard
