      </AsciiMap>
      <p>Finally, return to the four-way intersection and take the left path. Proceed up the steps to the left, and search above for a hidden chest which contains a <Tag type="item">Celestial Dew</Tag>. Go back down the steps and up through another tiny, dark passage until you reach a wide open area. Search the center of the area for a hidden chest which contains the <Tag type="key">Divine Pact</Tag> for <Tag type="char">Eruca</Tag>. Head right along the path to a tiny room with a chest which contains a <Tag type="item">Divine Water</Tag>.</p>
      <p>Return to the open area and take the upper path to the next room. Follow path up, then left two rooms to a fork. The lower path leads to an isolated chest which contains <Tag type="item">2 Special Teas</Tag>. Go back to the fork, and follow the right path until you reach a + shaped area. At the top is another floor panel with a switch that will open the door above. I would strongly recommend having two maxed out Mana Burst gauges before moving on. Then, return to the save point and head up to find the <Tag type="key">Beast Mark</Tag> and your next test.</p>
      <BossCard name="Shadow" weakness="Fire">
        <p><strong>Strategy:</strong> Have <Tag type="char">Eruca</Tag> cast <Tag type="skill">Magic Boost</Tag> on <Tag type="char">Aht</Tag>. Have her lay <Tag type="skill">Flamestar Traps</Tag> in the back row. Then use <Tag type="skill">Push Assault</Tag> and <Tag type="skill">Right Assault</Tag> to defeat him quickly.</p>
      </BossCard>
      <p>For defeating him, you will win the <Tag type="key">Beast Mark</Tag>. That&#x27;s it. Everything&#x27;s done. Might as well pack our bags and go home. Or I could be speaking too soon.</p>
      <BossCard name="Guardian" weakness="None">
        <p><strong>Strategy:</strong> Another giant spider, except this one can kill you in one turn. This is why I recommended having your maxed out Mana Burst gauges. Use two of them to use <Tag type="skill">Turn Break</Tag> on its first two turns, giving you nine consecutive turns. <Tag type="char">Stocke</Tag> should lead by using a <Tag type="item">Magic Herb</Tag> on <Tag type="char">Eruca</Tag> for casting <Tag type="skill">G-Frost</Tag>. This is where <Tag type="char">Aht</Tag> will really shine. Her new <Tag type="skill">Dancing Death</Tag> ability can REALLY drive up the combo bonus. Arrange the remaining 8 turns as follows: Dancing Death, Fire, Dancing Death, Fire, Dancing Death, G-Frost, G-Frost, G-Frost to defeat the <Tag type="boss">Guardian</Tag>.</p>
      </BossCard>
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Overcoming the Trial">
        <p>With the <Tag type="key">Beast Mark</Tag>, you could get past the roadblock in Alternate History, but since we&#x27;re almost done here, we might as well wrap things up. Talk to <Tag type="char">Bergas</Tag> to be prompted for a decision on how to assault <Tag type="place">Granorg</Tag>. Choosing to &quot;Lead the way&quot; will unlock the [Premature Invasion] ending.</p>
      </Callout>
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: The Final Defense">
        <p>Before moving on, return to Historia with the <Tag type="key">Beast Mark</Tag> to unlock your final Mana Burst. Return to &quot;The Three Contracts&quot; and teach the new Pact to <Tag type="char">Eruca</Tag>. Then, return to the previous decision point, choose to &quot;Wait for the Gutrals&quot;, and events will proceed more favorably this time.</p>
      </Callout>
    </div>
  </ChapterCard>

